{
  "case_id": "2021-20-601",
  "document_hash": "b5ffe750859666f3edaa287090b55221d3655ba55c9dbc77e7f9029c6a3f24a2",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Attorney General Matthew Kuhn (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2021-20-601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b5ffe750859666f3edaa287090b55221d3655ba55c9dbc77e7f9029c6a3f24a2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b5ffe7508596-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Second, the panel refused to consider Kentucky's sovereign interests in enforcing and defending its law. To be clear, the panel did not merely weigh factors to arrive at its timeliness holding. It affirmatively treated Kentucky's sovereign interests as irrelevant to that inquiry."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b5ffe750859666f3edaa287090b55221d3655ba55c9dbc77e7f9029c6a3f24a2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b5ffe7508596-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Mr. Kuhn, you -- there isn't much law for appellate intervention, so what do we rely on? Do we rely on Rule 24, which doesn't really apply? Would you give us -- what would be your strongest case that we should have a basis for this intervention that's not in the rules of appellate procedure?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2021-20-601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b5ffe750859666f3edaa287090b55221d3655ba55c9dbc77e7f9029c6a3f24a2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b5ffe7508596-0001-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Two days later, we filed a 20-page motion to intervene on behalf of the Commonwealth."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b5ffe750859666f3edaa287090b55221d3655ba55c9dbc77e7f9029c6a3f24a2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b5ffe7508596-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: And, finally, the Sixth Circuit seemed to rely primarily not on the jurisdictional issue but on intervention, that the reason it would not grant intervention was because of prejudice, and it based that prejudice to you on an argument, a third-party standing argument, that the Attorney General was raising."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Secretary",
      "case_id": "2021-20-601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b5ffe750859666f3edaa287090b55221d3655ba55c9dbc77e7f9029c6a3f24a2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b5ffe7508596-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. KOLBI-MOLINAS: The prejudice was that the argument had been waived. The Secretary had not made the argument about third-party standing on appeal. It had been part of the district court judgment. The district court had held that the plaintiffs had third-party standing. The Secretary chose not to appeal it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-20-601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b5ffe750859666f3edaa287090b55221d3655ba55c9dbc77e7f9029c6a3f24a2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b5ffe7508596-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: But -- but we didn't talk about intervention in Torres, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b5ffe750859666f3edaa287090b55221d3655ba55c9dbc77e7f9029c6a3f24a2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b5ffe7508596-0003-0006",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Otherwise, a jurisdictional rule, as this Court held in Torres, would be meaningless."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-601",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b5ffe750859666f3edaa287090b55221d3655ba55c9dbc77e7f9029c6a3f24a2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b5ffe7508596-0003-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 81,
        "start": 81
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 11:14 a.m., the case was submitted.)"
    },
